	)
	(text "WHY THIS SHEET EXISTS. The UWB array reports a tag RELATIVE to its own antenna frame.\nGeoreferencing needs WHERE the station is (GNSS) and WHICH WAY it faces (heading).\nGNSS now comes from the nRF9151 on the connectivity sheet (MAX-M10S U9 removed\n2026-11-17, with its C32/C33/C34, which decoupled only U9). Heading stays here:\n  U10 LIS3MDL magnetometer -> heading\n  U11 LIS2DH accelerometer -> pitch/roll for tilt-compensating U10, and INT1 knock /\n      move detect (a moved station silently invalidates both fix and heading).\nPosition without heading gives a circle of tag locations, not a point -- do not drop U10."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 22.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e5307542-914b-4264-a838-4c83638ed62c")
	)
	(text "MAGNETOMETER LAYOUT KEEP-OUT (U10) -- this decides heading accuracy, not the part.\nST: \"Keep currents higher than 10 mA a few millimeters away from the sensor IC\"\n(DocID024204 Rev 4 sec 4.3). This board has three much bigger sources:\n  1. BUCK INDUCTOR (TPS62A02 L1, regulation sheet): switching AC field + DC bias.\n     Keep U10 >= 25 mm from L1 and its SW node loop; never on the opposite side under it.\n  2. LTE ANTENNA FEED (nRF9151, connectivity): up to ~23 dBm TX and the PA supply\n     current bursts on +VBAT_LTE. Keep U10 >= 20 mm from the LTE feed / matching network\n     and from the +VBAT_LTE trace and its bulk caps.\n  3. BATTERY CURRENT LOOPS (power_bms): cell, AO3401A Q1, MCP73871 VBAT/OUT and\n     charge paths carry 0.5-1 A. Keep U10 out of the loop area; route those\n     out-and-return pairs tightly so their fields cancel.\nAlso: no steel near U10 (screws, standoffs, SMA bodies are often nickel-plated brass,\nwhich is fine; plated steel is not), no ground-plane splits that force return\ncurrents under it. U11 sits beside U10 -- tilt compensation assumes the two share\none rigid frame, and its axes must be documented relative to U10 in firmware.\nHard/soft-iron calibration is per build and IN the enclosure (decisions.md, Open).\nDistances above are engineering guidance, not ST figures -- verify by logging\nheading with the LTE modem and charger cycling at bring-up."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 200.66 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e750421d-ff4d-4dbe-af85-f42a3dd75419")
	)
